{"id":"c0bb7c1368e3c7b0","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-positive-operator.md","title":"Positive Operator","display":"df-positive-operator — Positive Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-positive-operator","aliases":["58-df-positive-operator","Positive Operator"],"display":"df-positive-operator — Positive Operator","depends_on":["[[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-positive-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-positive-operator</span><span>Positive Operator</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-positive-operator — Positive Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6da70a87682c611a\" href=\"?note=6da70a87682c611a\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md\">../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\mathcal H\\in V\">\\(T,\\mathcal H\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal H_{(-)}:V\\rightharpoonup V\">\\(\\mathcal H_{(-)}:V\\rightharpoonup V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6da70a87682c611a\" href=\"?note=6da70a87682c611a\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md\">../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S\\subseteq V^2\\cup V\">\\(\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S\\subseteq V^2\\cup V\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\land\\forall v\\in\\mathcal H\\;\\left(\\langle T(v),v\\rangle_{\\mathcal H}\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\land\\forall v\\in\\mathcal H\\;\\left(\\langle T(v),v\\rangle_{\\mathcal H}\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H_T)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H_T)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Positive operator: self-adjoint with nonnegative spectrum; yields positive quadratic form</li>\n<li>For positive <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>, one may define <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|T|=\\mathrm{PosSqrt}_S(T^*T)\">\\(|T|=\\mathrm{PosSqrt}_S(T^*T)\\)</span> as a derived operator.</li>\n<li>Polar decomposition: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T = U|T|\">\\(T = U|T|\\)</span> where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> unitary on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}}|T|\">\\(\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}}|T|\\)</span></li>\n<li>Monotone: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0 \\leq S \\leq T\">\\(0 \\leq S \\leq T\\)</span> in positive operators means <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T-S \\geq 0\">\\(T-S \\geq 0\\)</span>; ordered Banach space</li>\n<li>Positive-semidefinite, entrywise nonnegative, and totally positive matrices are distinct notions.</li>\n<li>The unary form uses the Hilbert space designated by the operator object and is retained for downstream compatibility.</li>\n<li>The imported self-adjoint predicate is built from the library's bounded adjoint predicate, so its operator domain is the whole designated Hilbert space; no independent partial-domain symbol is introduced here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Simon, Trace Ideals and Their Applications</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"6da70a87682c611a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"6da70a87682c611a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,\\mathcal H\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal H_{(-)}:V\\rightharpoonup V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S\\subseteq V^2\\cup V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\land\\forall v\\in\\mathcal H\\;\\left(\\langle T(v),v\\rangle_{\\mathcal H}\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}operator}\\vdash\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S(T,\\mathcal H_T)","display":true},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"|T|=\\mathrm{PosSqrt}_S(T^*T)","display":false},{"tex":"T = U|T|","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}}|T|","display":false},{"tex":"0 \\leq S \\leq T","display":false},{"tex":"T-S \\geq 0","display":false}],"bytes":1894,"backlinks":[{"id":"f9fa657af9512258","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PositiveOperator}_S$ (positive operator predicate, see [[58-df-positive-operator]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-970","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-positive-operator.md|58-df-positive-operator]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["6da70a87682c611a"]}